## Interface: 16001, 120105
## Title: Loot
## Notes: Loot on a page of Sane UI's journal: what a corpse, a chest or a catch holds, taken with a click or at once by your own rules (coins, quest items, a list of your own, everything up to a quality). A master looter's menu to give a thing away, cards for your group's rolls with who chose what, a feed of what you and your group receive, and a page that finds room when your bags are full.
## Author: Saneroki
## Version: 0.3.0
## Category: Sane UI
## Group: SaneUI
## Dependencies: SaneUI
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\INV_Misc_Bag_10
## X-License: MIT

# The module's own table, its words, sizes and settings. First: the other files will add to that table.
Loot.lua
# What the open loot holds, read from the game into plain lines; what is taken at once
Slots.lua
# The game's sentences about loot (received, rolled, coins) read back into their parts
Chat.lua
# The game's own loot window and roll frames out of sight while ours stand in, and back
Game.lua
# One line of the loot window: a thing's picture in its pencil slot, its name and a note under it
Row.lua
# The loot window, at the mouse or where Edit Mode placed it
Window.lua
# A master looter's menu: who may have the thing, and a roll for it
Master.lua
# With your bags full: what the thing is worth, and the least worth of yours to make room
Full.lua
# A card for each roll of your group: Need, Greed, Pass, the time left, who chose what
Rolls.lua
# What you and your group receive, rising over the world and fading
Feed.lua
